# Loss Tracking System Context Fix Guide

## Current Context Issues
This document addresses the inconsistencies in the Loss Tracking System implementation context. The following issues have been identified:

1. Core mechanics file shows Loss Tracking System as [to-do] while implementation is in progress
2. Loss Tracking System implementation file shows Battalion Loss Tracking as [test-failing] while tests are implemented
3. Active working context shows progress on Loss Rate Calculation while implementation file does not reflect this

## Verification Steps

### 1. Verify Test Status
Run the Loss Tracking System tests to determine actual status:
```bash
cd mobile
npm test -- -t 'Loss Tracking System'
```

Expected results:
- All Battalion Loss Tracking tests should pass
- All Loss Rate Calculation tests should pass
- Loss Comparison Analytics tests should not exist or should fail

### 2. Verify Implementation Code
Check the actual implementation in BattleStateManager.ts:
```bash
grep -r "battalion.*loss" mobile/src/battle/core/BattleStateManager.ts
grep -r "loss.*rate" mobile/src/battle/core/BattleStateManager.ts
```

Expected results:
- Battalion Loss Tracking methods should be implemented
- Loss Rate Calculation methods should be implemented
- Loss Comparison Analytics methods should not be implemented

## Fix Procedure

### 1. Update Core Mechanics File
Update the Loss Tracking System status in core-mechanics.mdc:
```diff
- ## Loss Tracking System [to-do]
+ ## Loss Tracking System [in-progress]
```

### 2. Update Implementation File
Update the loss-tracking-system-implementation.mdc file:

```markdown
